# Agentic framework (Cursor rules)

You are working in a repo that uses the `.agentic/` agentic development framework.

## Always read first
- `AGENTS.md` (if present)
- `CONTEXT_PACK.md`
- `STATUS.md`
- `spec/OVERVIEW.md`
- `spec/FEATURES.md`
- `spec/NFR.md` (if constraints apply)
- Relevant `/spec/*` sections, including `spec/acceptance/F-####.md` for the feature you are changing

## Agent Mode (model selection)
Check `agent_mode` in STACK.md: `premium` | `balanced` (default) | `economy`
Custom models: check `models:` section. Full docs: `.agentic/workflows/agent_mode.md`

## Must-follow behavior
- Follow `.agentic/agents/shared/agent_operating_guidelines.md`.
- **Follow programming standards**: `.agentic/quality/programming_standards.md`
  - Security first (validate input, parameterized queries, no hardcoded secrets)
  - Clear naming (descriptive, not cryptic)
  - Small functions (<50 lines)
  - Explicit error handling
- **Follow testing standards**: `.agentic/quality/test_strategy.md`
  - Test happy path, edge cases, invalid input
  - Test time-based behavior with mock clocks
  - Use descriptive test names
- Keep changes small; prefer incremental diffs.
- Add/update tests for new/changed logic.
- Update `STATUS.md` after progress and keep specs truthful.

## Developer UX
- Always end with: what changed, what's next, and what you need from the user.

## Autonomous modes
- `ag auto verify` — test-fix loop until green (add `--visual` for AI screenshot review)
- `ag auto task F-XXXX` — implements feature from ACs, creates PR
- `ag auto crunch` — batch processes all planned features
- `ag auto epic F-XXXX` — schedules epic's children with non-blocking reviews
- `ag auto pipeline --vision "text"` — end-to-end: vision → features → epic → implement → ship
- `ag auto verify-framework` — self-test: build example projects, detect & fix framework bugs

Workflows, gates, delegation: run `ag` commands or see `.agentic/agents/shared/auto_orchestration.md`

